var ROUTE=[["Narshe — the march on the frozen esper",1,"",["Terra starts at level 3 and should STAY there — no stat espers exist yet, so every level gained now is wasted. Her level also drags the party average down, which is what sets each later recruit's join level. Holding her here is a real cost paid up front for a better roster later.","Terra, Biggs and Wedge march north through town in Magitek Armor. You massively outclass everything here — Fire Beam wins every fight. No equipment changes are possible yet.","There is a save point immediately inside the mine. Save, then check the fence a little further in to trigger Ymir.","Ymir: attack the HEAD (1,600 HP) only. The head ducks in and out of the shell on a timer — if you attack while it is hiding, it counters with Megavolt. Just wait for it to surface. It has no weakness, so anything works, but Terra's Magitek Missile hits hardest.","Do not chase the Shell (50,000 HP). Both Ymir bestiary entries register from the one win.","After the fight, check the frozen esper at the back. The event carries you straight to a house in Narshe.","Do not try to explore Narshe yet — the town is closed to you and there is nothing here to take. Town cleanup opens up much later."],[],[0,59],[],"once",null,1,null],["Narshe — escape through the western mines",1,"Leaving for Figaro Castle",["Terra wakes in Arvis's house. Check the CLOCK for an Elixir, then talk to the man by the bed to continue. You leave through the back door into the western mines.","Past the save point are two chests holding Phoenix Down and Sleeping Bag. LEAVE THEM CLOSED — in the World of Ruin they upgrade to Guard Bracelet and Elixir.","Keep going deeper until the pursuers catch up and Terra falls through a trapdoor. Locke and the moogles arrive and the Moogle Defense begins.","STRIP MOG'S MYTHRIL SPEAR AND MYTHRIL SHIELD during the defense — open the menu between waves. Mog is not a real recruit yet and leaves with whatever he is wearing. Locke can use the shield now and Edgar wants that spear at Figaro Castle; miss it and you buy one for 800 gil in Nikeah instead.","Switch between the three parties, clear the enemies, and push south. If any monster reaches Terra it is game over.","Guard Leader (420 HP, weak to Poison) waits at the south end. Clear the trash with one party and swap to a fresh one before engaging him. Locke can steal a Mythril Knife.","Guard Leader is the first of your combat-critical Rages — make sure the entry registers.","Wererat, Spritzer and Bandit are limited-time entries inside these mines. Spritzer reappears on Mt. Kolts but vanishes later too, so it is safer to take it here.","You escape near the Narshe entrance. The town stays blocked, but the Adventuring School by the gate is open — take the Potion, Sleeping Bag and Ether, and fight the Silver Lobo in the east room.","Head south across the desert to Figaro Castle."],[],[1],[0,1],"",null,null,null],["Figaro Castle",1,"",["Name Edgar, then talk to him in the throne room.","Go back outside, into the west-side room, and down the stairs to the west building. Talk to the high priestess by the bed.","Return to the throne room and talk to Edgar again — Kefka arrives.","Control switches to Edgar: talk to the two soldiers who came in, then Kefka, then Locke. Control switches to Terra: go with Locke to the east building and talk to him again. Control returns to Edgar: talk to Kefka, then the soldier on the north side.","Collect the shop-area chests (Gold Needle west, Potion and Antidote east) and the Phoenix Down in the northern tower. SKIP the basement — those chests are World of Ruin only.","Buy Bioblaster and Noiseblaster from the east shop. Auto Crossbow is given to you, so you never need to buy Edgar a weapon: Tools ignore his Attack stat entirely.","Escaping the castle forces two Magitek Armor (210 HP, weak to Lightning). Edgar's Auto Crossbow ends it. Terra's Fire scene is automatic in the Pixel Remaster.","A Chocobo Stable sits southwest of where the castle surfaces — 100 gil a ride if you want faster overworld travel.","Head southeast for South Figaro Cave."],[],[],[2],"",[["Noiseblaster",500,"Edgar — Confuse on all enemies, never misses",""],["Bioblaster",750,"Edgar — Poison damage to all enemies",""]],null,null],["South Figaro Cave — first crossing",1,"Entering the Returners' Hideout",["Talk to the soldier at the cave entrance, then head in. There is no boss here — it is a straight walk through to South Figaro.","Foper, Hornet and Urok are limited-time entries. The cave's encounter table is REPLACED later in the story, so win at least one fight against each before you leave.","All three chests here upgrade if you leave them: the two Ethers become Thunder Rod and Hi-Ether, and the Phoenix Down becomes X-Potion. You come back through with Celes, so leaving them is cheap.","Exit to South Figaro."],["g1"],[2],[3],"",null,null,null],["South Figaro",1,"",["Shopping and looting stop — there is no required story event here.","In the NORTHWEST mansion, go to the left room on the second floor and check the bookcase for a hidden staircase down into the secret passage. You can reach part of it right now.","Take Hyper Wrist and Hermes Sandals from the prison room down there, plus the 500 / 1,000 / 1,500 gil chests in the clock room. Hyper Wrist is the prize — it multiplies Strength by 1.5, and Auto Crossbow loses no power from the back row, so back-row Edgar with Hyper Wrist carries this whole act.","Sweep the outdoor chests. Most of them upgrade in the World of Ruin, but South Figaro is fully revisitable, so take what you need now.","Spend on ARMOR, not weapons. Locke gets Main Gauche free on Mt. Kolts and Edgar does not care about his weapon at all.","Sprint Shoes (1,500 gil) still stack on top of the Pixel Remaster's built-in dash if you want the speed.","Shadow is in the pub — talk to him for a scene. He cannot join yet.","Head northeast toward Mt. Kolts, stopping at Duncan's Cabin on the way."],[],[],[4,5],"",[["Sprint Shoes",1500,"Any character — doubles movement speed, stacks with the built-in dash",""],["Kenpo Gi",250,"Locke — Def 34",""],["Plumed Hat",250,"Anyone — Def 14",""],["Heavy Shield",400,"Terra / Locke / Edgar — Def 22",""]],null,null],["Duncan's Cabin",1,"",["A small house on the world map NORTH of South Figaro — you enter it from the overworld, not from inside town. This is Duncan's home, Sabin's master; it is not Sabin's house.","Not required for the story. Go in for the Potion by the stove and a short scene about Edgar and Sabin.","Step back outside and an old man appears — talk to him for the story about Duncan.","This place matters again in the World of Ruin: it is where Sabin learns Phantom Rush, his final Blitz. It does NOT disappear."],[],[],[6],"",null,null,null],["Mt. Kolts",1,"",["Head northeast from South Figaro into the mountains.","Two hidden passages hold the good gear: Main Gauche southeast of the main cave, and GIGAS GLOVE northeast of it. Do not leave without the glove.","Gigas Glove raises physical damage 25%. Stack it with the Hyper Wrist from South Figaro on Edgar, put him in the back row, and let Auto Crossbow do the work.","There are also two Tents — one through the first cave past the bridge, one in the cave after the boss.","From the cave map with the save point, exit EAST to trigger Vargas.","Vargas (11,600 HP, weak to Poison) opens with two Ipooh (360 HP each, weak to Fire). Kill the Ipooh first — Fire and Auto Crossbow both clear them fast — then start on Vargas.","Once Vargas is damaged enough, Sabin jumps in. Damage him a little more and the Blitz tutorial appears; use Raging Fist to end the fight. The Blitz is what finishes it, not raw damage.","Steal Mythril Claws from Vargas if you have turns to spare — that is Sabin's weapon and it costs 800 gil otherwise.","Sabin joins for real after the fight. Continue north to the Returners' Hideout."],[],[60],[7],"",null,null,null],["Returners' Hideout",1,"Jumping into the Lethe River",["Talk to Banon; control switches to Terra. Talk to Locke, Edgar and Sabin, then the man by the entrance to head outside.","Loot the whole hideout before you trigger anything — Air Knife, White Cape, Knight's Code and Green Cherry in the storeroom, Phoenix Downs in Terra's room and the storeroom, Hi-Potion in Banon's room, Antidote and Ether along the north wall. NONE of this is available in the World of Ruin.","BANON'S QUESTION decides which relic you get here. Answer YES for GAUNTLET; answer NO three times for GENJI GLOVE. You get one, not both.","Gauntlet holds one weapon two-handed for 2x power. Genji Glove dual-wields for two attacks per turn.","THIS IS A PREFERENCE CALL, NOT A MISSABLE ONE — both types show up again as ordinary chests later. Gauntlet appears in Yeti's Cave and in Kefka's Tower; Genji Glove appears on the lava island in the Cave to the Sealed Gate and in the Dreamscape's second train car. Whichever you pass up here, you can still have one before the end.","The event then drops the party straight into the Lethe River. There is no coming back."],["g2"],[],[8],"wob",null,null,null],["Lethe River",1,"Reaching the scenario split",["The raft carries the party automatically. At the FIRST fork every path converges — take Straight for the shortest run to the save point. At the SECOND fork go LEFT.","Check the bucket beside the save point to fully restore HP and MP.","Lesser Lopros, Nautiloid and Exocite exist ONLY on this river. You ride it once more during Terra's scenario and then never again — that is your whole window for these three entries.","Ultros (3,000 HP, weak to Fire and Lightning) ends the ride. Tentacle can drop a front-row character outright, so put EVERYONE in the back row.","Auto Crossbow, Aura Cannon and Fire carry the damage. Banon should use Pray every single turn — he is your only healer and his level was set by the party average.","After Ultros the story splits three ways. You control a moogle and pick by talking to Locke, Terra or Sabin. Any order works; this route runs Locke, then Terra, then Sabin."],[],[26,61],[],"once",null,1,null],["Locke's scenario — occupied South Figaro",1,"Scenario end",["Locke is alone in an occupied town. The whole route is a chain of DISGUISES, each stolen from a fight.","1. Item shop: talk to the merchant by the clock to start a battle, then STEAL his clothes for the merchant disguise.","2. Go down the stairs in front of the item shop and into the house — as a merchant, the boy downstairs lets you past.","3. Out the back door, up the stairs on the northeast wall, then follow the wall west. Fight the green-uniformed soldier and STEAL the soldier outfit.","4. As a soldier, talk to the guard blocking the path just above the chocobo stable. He steps aside — head south into the pub.","5. In the pub basement, steal the merchant's clothes again. This also gets you the CIDER.","6. Back to the boy's house through the rear, upstairs, and give the old man the Cider.","7. Talk to the boy downstairs and answer the password COURAGE. He opens the secret passage.","HEAVY ARMOR (495 HP, weak to Lightning and Water) is only here and as a rare brown-squad formation at the Battle of Narshe — much easier to take now. Steal an Iron Helm from it if you can.","Follow the hidden route to the mansion on the north side of town, into the left room on 2F, and behind the left bookcase to go down.","Do NOT use the merchant/Cider duplication glitch."],[],[3],[],"once",null,null,null],["Locke's scenario — South Figaro secret passage",1,"Scenario end",["Try the FIRST DOOR you see in the passage. The event inside brings in Celes — talk to her to free her and she joins.","Check the soldier sitting in the chair for the OLD CLOCK KEY. You cannot progress without it.","If you skipped the jail chests on your first visit to town, get them now: walk down from the first passage to the stairs for Hyper Wrist and Hermes Sandals. In the Pixel Remaster the old hidden route is drawn as an ordinary passage, so just keep walking down where the path continues.","There is a save point in the room to the right of where Celes was held.","In the far-right room, wind the clock in the upper-right corner. With the Old Clock Key a door appears and lets you through.","The area past it is full of hidden rooms and side paths. DO NOT LEAVE WITHOUT THE RIBBON — it blocks nearly every status in the game and stays useful for the rest of the run. Hi-Ether and X-Potion are down there with it.","The later escape map holds Iron Armor, Great Sword, Heavy Shield and Earring.","Commander and Vector Hound live here, but both come back in the World of Ruin basements, so neither is urgent.","Leave the mansion and head northwest on the world map to South Figaro Cave."],[],[],[16],"once",null,null,null],["Locke's scenario — South Figaro Cave with Celes",1,"Scenario end",["The encounter table has been REPLACED. Cartagra, Acrophies and Gold Bear are here now and vanish for good after this route.","TWO of the three chests keep upgrading; the third is already final. LEAVE the chest UP THE NORTHWEST STAIRS (Thunder Rod now, HERO'S RING in the World of Ruin) and the one at the EAST END of the main cave (Ether now, Hi-Ether in the WoR). TAKE the WEST-END chest — it is an X-Potion and that is as good as it gets, so there is nothing to save it for.","Move through toward the Figaro Castle side. Tunnel Armor ambushes you near the exit.","Tunnel Armor (1,300 HP, weak to Lightning and Water): have CELES USE RUNIC EVERY TURN to eat its magic — that is what makes this fight safe. Locke attacks with the Hyper Wrist equipped, and dual-wields if you took the Genji Glove.","STEAL AN AIR KNIFE from Tunnel Armor at 87.5% — that is a genuinely good weapon this early. It also drops an Elixir at 100%.","Let Locke handle healing items when HP gets shaky. Beating Tunnel Armor ends Locke's scenario."],["g3"],[4],[17],"once",null,null,null],["Terra's scenario — Lethe River to Narshe",1,"Scenario end",["Terra's route restarts on the Lethe River with no boss and no forks — just a few normal battles. This is your LAST ride down the river, so if Lesser Lopros, Nautiloid or Exocite are still missing, farm them here.","You land on the world map; Narshe is directly north.","The front gate is barred by Imperial soldiers. From the town entrance go WEST and check the rocks to slip into the mines.","A moving light marks the correct path through the small maze inside — follow it rather than guessing.","The moogle-room chest holds a Rune Blade now and a RIBBON in the World of Ruin. Leave it closed.","Valeor and Wild Rat live only in these western mines — register them before you leave.","Exit through the back, enter the house, and talk to Arvis. Terra's scenario ends."],[],[5],[9],"once",null,null,null],["Sabin's scenario — the Cabin",1,"Leaving for the Imperial Camp",["Sabin starts on the world map with a Cabin nearby. Talk to SHADOW in the yard and bring him along — he is your damage for this entire scenario.","BUY 99 SHURIKEN at 30 gil each. Shadow's Throw ignores defense, never misses, and loses nothing from the back row. This is the cheapest damage in the World of Balance and the single best purchase of Act I.","The chocobo-riding item seller in the yard wanders off, but stepping inside the house and back out respawns him — repeat until your stock is full.","Head southeast to the Imperial Camp."],[],[],[],"",[["Shuriken",30,"Shadow — Throw, ignores defense, never misses. Buy 99.",""],["Invisibility Scroll",200,"Shadow — Throw for Invisible on himself",""],["Shadow Scroll",400,"Shadow — Throw for Image on himself",""]],null,null],["Sabin's scenario — Imperial Camp and Doma Castle",1,"The third Kefka conversation",["An event starts near the entrance; after the soldiers finish, control switches to Cyan. Talk to the black-armoured soldier in front of the castle and spam Fang to win.","Back as Sabin: the chest in the tent right of the entrance can be KICKED open for a Star Pendant with no fight at all.","Head south for the Leo and Kefka scene. You fight Kefka twice and each fight ends after a single hit — just keep chasing.","CLEAR EVERY CHEST BEFORE THE THIRD KEFKA CONVERSATION. Green Beret, Mythril Glove and Barrier Ring vanish permanently once that scene starts, and boarding the Magitek armour afterwards locks the camp for good.","The Green Beret chest spawns SATELLITE (1,800 HP, weak to Lightning and Water). It exists nowhere else in the game. Heal first, put Sabin and Shadow in the back row, and use Aura Cannon plus Shuriken. It drops a second Green Beret at 100%.","Reach the Barrier Ring chest by dropping down from behind the tent that held Satellite.","Control switches to Cyan: go to the king's room on Doma Castle 1F, speak to the king, then the room on the right where his family is.","Only the REMEDY is obtainable in Doma Castle right now. The rest unlock after the Imperial banquet if you get the soldiers to withdraw, or in the World of Ruin regardless of how the banquet goes.","Back as Sabin, talk to Cyan and fight through the Imperial soldiers. The party then boards Magitek armour and escapes.","Head south from the world map to the Phantom Forest."],["g4"],[7],[10,11],"once",null,null,null],["Sabin's scenario — Phantom Forest and Phantom Train",1,"Defeating the Phantom Train",["The forest loops if you take a wrong path. At the fork, take the UPPER-RIGHT path and you reach the train almost immediately.","Poplium appears only in the Phantom Forest. The FOREST can be walked back into later — it is the TRAIN that is one-visit-only — so this is not the hard wall the gate makes it look like. jinsoku still lists Poplium as lost once the story advances, and nobody has pinned down where that line actually falls, so register it while you are standing in it.","On the train, go to the REAR car first: recruit a Ghost if you want one, and save.","Leaving the first car and coming back makes Ghosts wander the interior; one of them is an item seller.","BRING A PHOENIX DOWN. The Phantom Train (1,900 HP) is undead with no Instant Death immunity — a single Phoenix Down kills it outright.","Ghosts block the door in the frontmost reachable car. Talk, fight, then step outside to trigger the scene that throws the party forward.","Enter the car Sabin lands in and pull the lever to detach the rear cars, then enter again and pull it once more to continue.","Sit at the middle table in the DINING CAR to eat — it fully restores HP and MP for free.","In the small room past the dining car, one chest starts a fight with SIEGFRIED (100 HP). He is free and drops a Green Cherry.","In the four-chest room in the third car from the front, the FAR-LEFT chest spawns APPARITION (1,500 HP). It is undead with no death immunity — Phoenix Down kills it instantly and it drops a Hyper Wrist at 100%.","OVERSOUL only appears in the car with the second save point. If the entry is missing, grind there specifically.","The second car from the front has a save point. Rest before the boss.","In the engine room set the LEFT and RIGHT levers DOWN and the MIDDLE lever UP, then check the smokestack outside to start the fight.","Ghost, Cloud, Angel Whisper, Oversoul, Bomb, Living Dead, Apparition and Siegfried are all gone once you leave the train."],["g5"],[8,9,65],[12],"once",null,1,null],["Sabin's scenario — Baren Falls to Mobliz",1,"",["Loop around from the south and head east to Baren Falls, then walk to the cliff.","SHADOW LEAVES HERE if he is still with you. Take back anything you equipped on him — including leftover Shuriken.","Jumping off starts several consecutive battles. The Opinicus Fish are trivial (10 HP) but you are down to two characters, so watch your healing between fights.","Rhizopas (775 HP, weak to Lightning) ends the sequence and the party washes up on the Veldt.","Gau appears in a scene on the Veldt but does not join yet. Head east to Mobliz.","BUY DRIED MEAT (150 gil) at the Mobliz item shop — it is the only way to recruit Gau. Buy several.","Grab the Elixir on the house's first floor.","Win a battle on the Veldt and Gau may appear. Use Dried Meat on him and he joins.","Gau's Leap only works on the Veldt: he leaves the battle, and after a few more Veldt victories he returns, adding both the Leap battle's monsters and the return battle's monsters to his Rage list. The Veldt can only roll monsters you have ALREADY encountered.","Stray Cat is the easy early pick — its Rage is a 4x physical attack."],[],[10,63],[13],"once",null,1,null],["Sabin's scenario — Crescent Mountain Cave and Serpent Trench",1,"Arriving at Nikeah",["Head to Crescent Mountain Cave SOUTH OF THE VELDT. The story will not advance unless Gau is in the party.","Find the shiny treasure at the back, then jump from the cliff into the river to enter the Serpent Trench.","The Serpent Trench is a swimming current, not a raft — you are carried along automatically. There are two forks: go RIGHT AT BOTH to reach the cave rooms holding X-Potion and Green Beret.","Anguiform and Aspiran live only here, and Opinicus Fish only in Baren Falls. All three are gone after this.","The trench delivers you to Nikeah."],[],[11,64],[14],"once",null,1,null],["Sabin's scenario — Nikeah",1,"Boarding the ship",["Shopping only — there is no event here beyond boarding the ship.","MYTHRIL SPEAR (800 gil) is sold here. If you failed to strip Mog's spear back in the Narshe mines, this is where you replace it for Edgar.","Mythril Claws (800 gil) upgrades Sabin if you did not steal them from Vargas.","Take the Elixir in the Inn.","Board the ship from the port. Sabin's scenario ends and all three parties converge on Narshe."],[],[],[15],"",[["Mythril Spear",800,"Edgar — Attack 70, doubles Jump. Skip if you stripped Mog's.",""],["Mythril Claws",800,"Sabin — Attack 65. Skip if you stole them from Vargas.",""],["Silk Robe",600,"Terra / Celes — Def 39, Magic +1",""]],null,null],["Battle of Narshe",1,"Defeating Kefka",["All three scenarios converge and the party moves to the cliffs by the frozen esper. You split into THREE parties and protect Banon while pushing toward Kefka — if any enemy reaches him it is game over.","Stack your four strongest characters in ONE party and push with it. A solo party gets bullied by ordinary soldiers, so keep that one back and station the two-person party near Banon.","CELES BELONGS IN THE PUSHING PARTY. Runic eats Kefka's magic and turns the boss fight from annoying into routine.","Heavy Armor, Fidor, Corporal, Hunting Hound and Hell's Rider all disappear after this battle. This is your last window for all five.","Hell's Rider (1,300 HP, weak to Fire and Poison) stands in front of Kefka. It is tougher than the soldiers but not a real boss. Steal a MYTHRIL VEST from it.","Kefka (3,000 HP): keep Runic up and have everyone else attack. Sabin's Aura Cannon is plenty. He drops a PEACE RING at 100% and you can steal a Hi-Ether.","Terra leaves the party after the battle."],["g6"],[12],[],"once",null,null,null],["Narshe — the town opens",1,"",["With Kefka gone, the town of Narshe is finally open. This is the single richest treasure stop in the World of Balance so far.","THE SOUTHEAST STOREHOUSE ON THE UPPER LEDGE is the reason you are here: 5,000 gil, Earring, Thief's Knife, Reflect Ring, THIEF'S BRACER and HYPER WRIST.","Thief's Bracer doubles Locke's Steal success rate — with the steal list only getting better from here, take it before anything else. A second Hyper Wrist means two characters can run the Strength boost.","There is also an Elixir in the northwest building.","One chest in the treasure house stays locked. It opens after the Magitek Research Facility — you will be back.","The shops have restocked hard. Air Knife, Chain Flail and Moonring Blade are all here, and Chain Flail and Moonring Blade lose nothing from the back row.","Head south to Figaro Castle."],[],[],[18],"",[["Moonring Blade",2500,"Locke — Attack 95, full damage from the back row",""],["Chain Flail",2000,"Terra / Celes — Attack 86, full damage from the back row",""],["Air Knife",950,"Locke — Attack 76, Wind. Skip if you stole one from Tunnel Armor.",""],["Mythril Shield",1200,"Anyone — Def 27",""]],null,null],["Figaro Castle — the tunnel to Kohlingen",1,"",["Go down the stairs on the left inside the castle and talk to the old man in the basement. Choose to move toward KOHLINGEN and the castle submerges.","BUY DRILL AND FLASH for Edgar while you are here. Drill IGNORES DEFENSE and never misses — with Hyper Wrist and Gigas Glove on Edgar it is your best single-target damage for the entire middle of the game, and it stays relevant through the Floating Continent.","When the castle surfaces on the Kohlingen side, exit to the world map and head northwest.","Still skip the basement chests — they remain World of Ruin only."],[],[],[],"",[["Drill",3000,"Edgar — ignores Defense, never misses. The key purchase of Act I.",""],["Flash",1000,"Edgar — damage plus Blind to all enemies",""]],null,null],["Kohlingen",1,"",["Mostly an item stop. Jidoor's shops are better and they are close, so do not spend heavily here.","The northeast mansion has a chest you can only reach through the BACK DOOR — go in and check the left side for a GREEN BERET.","Rachel's house holds an Elixir.","Head north to Dragon's Neck Cabin."],[],[],[19],"",null,null,null],["Dragon's Neck Cabin",1,"",["The small house north of Kohlingen. Not required for the story.","Check the POT near the entrance for a HERO'S RING — it boosts both physical and magical damage by 25%. This is a top-tier relic that you are getting for free from a pot; do not walk past it.","Head south to Jidoor."],[],[],[20],"wob",null,null,null],["Jidoor",1,"",["No required story event — but the shops are the best you have seen and this is where your Narshe gil goes.","The AUCTION HOUSE is not running yet. It opens once the Blackjack is yours to fly, which is still several stops away.","Take the Ether from the northeast corner of Owzer's Mansion on 1F.","Sniper Eye (3,000 gil) makes physical attacks never miss. Earring (5,000 gil) multiplies magic damage by 1.25, and two of them by 1.5 — relevant the moment magicite arrives, which is the very next stop.","Head northeast, then follow the coast and mountains north. Zozo appears on the left."],[],[],[21],"",[["Sniper Eye",3000,"Anyone — physical attacks never miss",""],["Earring",5000,"Terra / Celes — magic damage x1.25, two give x1.5",""],["Mythril Vest",1200,"Anyone — Def 45",""],["Twist Headband",1600,"Locke / Sabin / Cyan / Shadow / Gau / Mog — Str +3, Sta +2, Spd +1",""]],null,null],["Zozo",1,"Defeating Dadaluma",["Zozo is called a town but it plays as a dungeon — random battles inside and a boss at the top. Nobody here tells the truth, including about the time.","CHAINSAW: check the clock in the northeast building and set it to 6:10:50. A hidden staircase opens to the chest. It hits hard and can instantly kill, though Drill remains the more dependable boss tool because it never misses.","Sweep the towers for Brigand's Glove, Burning Fist, Hermes Sandals, X-Potion and two Ethers before you climb.","To reach the top: enter the lower building and climb. When the stairs appear to stop outside, JUMP ACROSS to the building on the left, climb that side, then jump back to the building on the right.","Dadaluma (3,270 HP, weak to Poison) attacks near the top. Bioblaster or Gau's Wererat Rage hits the weakness, but straight damage is simpler — Drill with Hyper Wrist and Gigas Glove, plus Aura Cannon boosted by Earring or Hero's Ring.","STEAL FROM DADALUMA: Jeweled Ring at 87.5%, THIEF'S BRACER at 12.5%. If you want a second Thief's Bracer this is the only other source in the World of Balance.","Terra is in the room at the very top. Talk to her and the event hands you FOUR MAGICITE: Ramuh, Kirin, Siren and Cait Sith.","MAGICITE STARTS HERE. From now on characters learn magic by earning AP with magicite equipped — and more importantly, Strength and Magic do NOT rise on their own in FF6. They only rise from the level-up bonus of whatever magicite is equipped when a character levels. Every level from here on should be spent deliberately.","Talk to your party near the room entrance and you are returned to the Zozo entrance. Leave and head back to Jidoor."],[],[29,62],[22],"",null,1,null],["Opera House",1,"Stopping the weight",["Go to Owzer's Mansion at the north end of Jidoor, talk to the Impresario, and PICK UP THE LETTER HE DROPS. Without it there is no opera.","Leave town and head southeast to the Opera House. Talk to the Impresario by the entrance to start a long event.","As Locke, go to the dressing room and talk to Celes. Control switches to Celes — leave from the NORTH side of the room and step onto the stage.","CHOOSE THE OPERA LINES IN THIS ORDER: 'O my hero...', then 'I'm the darkness...', then 'Must my...'. A wrong pick restarts the whole scene.","The Pixel Remaster adds a button prompt at the end of the song — press confirm while it is on screen.","Check the letter in the hallway afterwards and report it to the Impresario.","A FIVE-MINUTE TIMER now runs. You only need to reach and talk to Ultros before it hits zero.","Go to the upper-right room and pull ONLY THE FAR-RIGHT LEVER. Then circle back, open the upper-left room, and head into the rafters.","Stunner (weak to Fire) and Goetia (weak to Ice) exist only in these rafters — register both while the timer runs.","Ultros (2,550 HP, weak to Lightning): Thundara folds him fast. Without it, summon Ramuh once and lean on Drill and Aura Cannon.","After the fight the airship carries the party to the southern continent on its own. You are NOT flying it — it sets you down by Albrook and you continue on foot."],["g7"],[13],[],"timed",null,null,null],["Albrook, Tzen and Maranda — on foot",1,"",["You are on the southern continent now and the Blackjack is not yours to steer. Everything here is reached by WALKING or by chocobo — there is no hopping back to the northern continent, so finish this sweep before you enter Vector.","Inside the Blackjack you can fully restore HP and MP and use the item shop. Use it as a free inn between towns.","ALBROOK sits right by the landing spot: Hi-Potion outside, Teleport Stone at the harbor, Ether in the weapon shop, Elixir in the pub/relic shop. Empty chests here stay empty forever, so do not hunt for more.","TZEN is north. The shops carry Hermes Sandals for permanent Haste.","A chocobo stable sits in the FOREST JUST EAST OF TZEN — useful for crossing to Maranda and Vector.","DO NOT GO HUNTING FOR THE SERAPH SELLER YET. Later there is a person in the trees at the UPPER RIGHT of Tzen's relic shop who sells the magicite, but he is no use — and not even standing there — until the Blackjack is yours to fly, which happens after the Magitek Research Facility. Come back then.","MARANDA is on the southwest peninsula. There is no story event here at all in the World of Balance — it is two chests, Holy Water and Remedy, plus shops.","Another unmarked chocobo stable sits in the lower-right of the forest southeast of Maranda.","When the sweep is done, head for Vector in the middle of the continent."],[],[],[23,24],"",[["Hermes Sandals",null,"Tzen — permanent Haste",""]],null,null],["Vector",1,"Entering the Magitek Research Facility",["SHOP AND REPAIR NOW. Once the old man lets you in you are LOCKED INSIDE until the facility is cleared, and there are four boss fights in there. Stock healing items and fix everyone's equipment before you climb the crates.","DO NOT PUSH NORTH. The north side of Vector leads toward the Imperial Palace and you can trigger GUARDIAN. This early version is an unwinnable wall. If the fight starts, run.","In the NORTHEAST part of the lower city an old man hides behind some crates. Talk to him and answer yes — he distracts the guard. THIS IS THE LOCK POINT: say yes and there is no more shopping.","Climb onto the crates, cross the beams, and enter the facility."],[],[],[],"",null,null,null],["Magitek Research Facility",1,"Meeting Setzer to leave",["THE FACILITY IS SEALED THE MOMENT YOU CLEAR IT. Every chest and every monster here is gone for good afterwards.","Head south inside and you will see Kefka loading espers onto a lift. Ride the lift down with them.","SAVE IN THE UPPER-LEFT ROOM before talking to Ifrit and Shiva — talking starts the fight.","Ifrit (3,300 HP, weak to Ice) and Shiva (3,000 HP, weak to Fire) cast constantly, so Celes's Runic earns its keep. After enough damage Ifrit swaps out for Shiva, but beating EITHER ONE ends the fight. You receive both magicite regardless.","FLAN only appears in the room with Ifrit and Shiva. Trapper, General, Destroyer and Lenergia only appear AFTER that fight. Onion Knight, Sergeant, Belzecue and Proto Armor are first-half only.","Continue through the door on the right — the crane in that room can carry you back up if you need it.","Climb the stairs and talk to the man ahead to fight NUMBER 024 (4,777 HP). Its weakness rotates and it tells you what is coming: Fire or Fira means it is weak to Ice, Blizzard or Blizzara means weak to Fire, Aqua Breath or Acid Rain means weak to Lightning. Or ignore the pattern entirely — Drill ignores Defense and Cyan's Fang does too. STEAL A RUNE BLADE at 87.5%, or gamble on BLOOD SWORD at 12.5%.","Sweep the floor chests: Flametongue, Thunder Blade, Icebrand, Golden Shield, Golden Helm, Golden Armor, Dragoon Boots, Zephyr Cloak, X-Potion, Remedy, Ether, Tent. The Golden set and Icebrand are real upgrades, not filler.","Pull the lever at the back of the lab. The event hands you SIX MORE MAGICITE: Maduin, Bismarck, Catoblepas, Phantom, Carbuncle and Unicorn.","Do not miss the STONEBLADE in the passage southwest of the last empty tube.","Celes leaves the party, then everyone rides the lift down to B1F with Cid."],["g8"],[14],[25,26],"once",null,null,null],["Minecart escape and the Cranes",1,"Boarding the Blackjack",["The small room after the lift has a save point. Check the bucket for a full HP and MP restore, then talk to Cid and board the minecart.","Magna Roader (purple) and Magna Roader (red) appear during the escape. CHECK YOUR PARTY LEADER before fighting the red one — it is the entry people miss.","Number 128 (3,276 HP, no weakness) ends the ride. Right Blade and Left Blade come with it, but they REVIVE after being destroyed and the main body punishes you for killing them. Ignore the arms and hit the body from turn one.","STEAL A KAZEKIRI from Number 128 at 12.5% — the first of two.","CHASER appears after the minecart and before the Cranes. It is a narrow window and easy to skip past.","Head for the Vector entrance to meet Setzer. The party is thrown straight into the Crane fight.","Crane (Left) has 1,800 HP, is weak to WATER, and ABSORBS LIGHTNING — never cast Thundara on it. Crane (Right) has 2,300 HP and is weak to Lightning.","Hit the right crane with Thundara and the left with Drill or Raging Fist. Steal Noiseblaster from the left and DEBILITATOR from the right if you want them early.","Beating both cranes ends Act I's locked stretch and the airship carries the party back to Zozo."],["g9"],[],[],"once",null,null,null],["Maduin flashback — the Esper World",1,"",["The story moves automatically to Zozo and the flashback begins. There is nothing to prepare and nothing missable here.","Help the woman lying on the north side of the village, let her rest in the bed, then talk to her again.","Enter the cave on the north side of the village and talk to Madeline.","Two years pass and Gestahl arrives with his soldiers. Talk to the elder, then talk to the fairy-like esper blocking the entrance.","Madeline runs out — follow her to the north cave and talk to her where she has fallen.","WHEN THE FLASHBACK ENDS Terra returns to the party AND THE BLACKJACK BECOMES YOURS TO FLY. This is the exact moment the World of Balance opens up. Everything gated on free flight starts now, and nothing before this point could have been done out of order."],[],[],[],"once",null,null,null],["Blackjack side trips — Jidoor auction and Tzen",1,"",["The Jidoor AUCTION HOUSE is finally running. It can offer two magicite: ZONA SEEKER for 10,000 gil and GOLEM for 20,000 gil. The stock is random — walk out of the AUCTION HOUSE and straight back in until the one you want appears. You do not need to leave town.","ZONA SEEKER IS THE ONE THAT MATTERS. Its level-up bonus is Magic +2, and paired with Bismarck's Strength +2 you can finally steer level-ups properly. Golem's Stamina +2 is a niche stat outside Regen.","Go back to TZEN and buy SERAPH for 3,000 gil from the seller hidden in the trees by the upper-right of the relic shop. It teaches Cura, Raise and Esuna.","Seraph drops to 10 gil in the World of Ruin, so this purchase is only worth it if you want those three spells for the rest of the World of Balance — which, given what is coming, you probably do.","The next story destination is Narshe."],[],[],[],"wob",[["Zona Seeker",10000,"Jidoor auction — magicite, level bonus Magic +2",""],["Golem",20000,"Jidoor auction — magicite, level bonus Stamina +2",""],["Seraph",3000,"Tzen — magicite teaching Cura, Raise and Esuna",""]],null,null],["Narshe — Banon, and recruiting Mog",1,"Leaving for the Cave to the Sealed Gate",["An event plays at the town entrance and the party meets Banon again. After it, the Cave to the Sealed Gate becomes the story destination.","RECRUIT MOG NOW. It is optional for the story and it is the most consequential optional thing in the World of Balance.","Climb the stairs on the right side of town, cross the upper ledge, and enter the small house at the lower right. Lone Wolf is inside.","Follow Lone Wolf into the northern mines. Take the passage on the RIGHT and keep following the path.","At the cliff Lone Wolf is holding Mog hostage. WAIT — after a moment Mog struggles and both end up hanging from the cliff. You save whichever one you TALK TO FIRST.","SAVE MOG. Saving Lone Wolf instead gets you a Gold Hairpin and Mog does not join here.","The Gold Hairpin halves magic MP costs, which sounds good until you remember Celestriad later reduces every spell to 1 MP. The real argument is WATER HARMONY: Mog can still be recruited in the World of Ruin, but that Dance can ONLY be learned in the World of Balance. Take Mog.","The locked chest in the treasure house is open now that the Magitek Research Facility is done — go back for it.","The shops have restocked again since the Battle of Narshe."],["g10"],[],[27],"",null,null,null],["Imperial Observation Post",1,"",["PUT TERRA IN THE PARTY before you come here — the story will not advance without her. The post is east of Vector.","The central building has a basement storehouse packed with treasure, but it is LOCKED for now. It opens only as a banquet reward, so do not waste time looking for another way in.","Pass straight through to the east and continue to the Cave to the Sealed Gate."],[],[],[],"wob",null,null,null],["Cave to the Sealed Gate",1,"Clearing the Esper Cave",["THIS CAVE CLOSES FOR GOOD once you clear the Esper Cave. Everything below is a one-shot.","ULTIMA WEAPON is the prize — the small hidden treasure room opened by SWITCH 5. Miss it and it is gone permanently. It scales with the wielder's current HP, so it may lose to your regular weapons right now; take it anyway, because it becomes one of the strongest weapons in the game.","The later part of the cave is full of switches, but reaching the end really only needs the SKULL-SHAPED SWITCH that slides the rock.","Sweep it thoroughly: Assassin's Dagger, KAZEKIRI (the second one), Heiji's Jitte, GENJI GLOVE, three Magicite Shards, Invisibility Scroll, Water Scroll, Hi-Ethers, Elixir and 293 gil.","Most of the enemies here are UNDEAD. Holy Water and Phoenix Down delete several outright, and Sabin's Aura Cannon hits hard because so many are weak to Holy.","Outcast, Provoker, Zombie Dragon, Antares and Lich are all limited. Provoker and Lich appear on the FIRST MAP ONLY — if you push past it without them you are done.","NINJA (1,650 HP, weak to Lightning and Holy) is the awkward one. Steal Angel Wings from it and it drops a Fuma Shuriken.","An event at the sealed gate puts you briefly against Kefka — deal some damage and it ends.","A shortcut path opens before the sealed gate leading back near the exit. Use it.","Leaving the Imperial Observation Post to the WEST triggers the airship event. After the crash landing, walk back to Vector."],["g11"],[15],[28],"once",null,null,null],["Imperial Palace banquet",1,"Banquet end",["You have FOUR MINUTES to talk to as many soldiers as possible — there are 24. The number you reach directly sets your reward.","EQUIP SPRINT SHOES. With them you can talk to the soldiers AND still collect every palace chest with time left.","DO NOT GO NEAR THE JAIL where Kefka is held. It burns a large chunk of the timer and gives you nothing.","Some soldiers start battles. The IMPERIAL ELITE only appears during this conversation event — it is your single window for that entry.","Palace chests: Alarm Earring, X-Potion, Ether, Gale Hairpin and Holy Water.","BANQUET ANSWERS for the best reward — 1: 'To our homelands.' 2: 'Leave him in jail.' 3: 'That was inexcusable.' 4: 'Celes is one of us!'","5: ask ALL THREE questions once each — 'Why did you start the war?', 'Why do you want peace now?', 'Why did you have me talk to your soldiers?' — then choose 'Let's talk about the espers.'","6: 'They have gone a bit too far...' 7: when asked which question you asked first, pick THE ONE YOU ACTUALLY ASKED FIRST.","Then 'Take a break.' Talk to the soldier and WIN THAT BATTLE WITHIN TWO MINUTES. Return to the table and choose yes to continue.","8: 'That your war is truly over.' Finally, say YES when Gestahl asks you to go to Crescent Island.","Score well enough and you receive TINTINNABULUM and WARD BANGLE, and the Imperial Observation Post storehouse unlocks."],["g12"],[16],[29],"once",null,null,null],["Imperial Observation Post storehouse",1,"Sailing for Thamasa",["Only open if your banquet score was high enough. If it opened, GO BACK FOR IT BEFORE CONTINUING — it is the largest single pile of treasure in the World of Balance and it is gone in the World of Ruin.","Thirteen chests: Angel Wings, Angel Ring, two Alarm Earrings, Reflect Ring, Hermes Sandals, Flametongue, X-Potion, Hi-Ether, two Elixirs, and 8,000 / 13,000 / 20,000 gil.","That is 41,000 gil in cash alone — enough to clear out the Jidoor auction if you skipped Golem or Zona Seeker.","One chest is inside the stove, which is exactly as findable as it sounds.","To continue, board the ship at the Albrook port and head for Thamasa."],[],[],[30,31],"wob",null,null,null],["Thamasa",1,"Staying at the inn",["Talk to General Leo on the ship once, then stay at the inn.","On arrival, go to the NORTHEAST house and talk to Strago.","COLLECT THAMASA NOW. Almost everything here is only available before the Esper Cave — Eye Drops, Gold Needle, Phoenix Down, Green Cherry and Echo Screen are scattered around town.","MEMENTO RING is a hidden chest in Relm's room on 2F — go around the LEFT WALL, near the left side of the table. Only Shadow and Relm can equip it, and it is the reason to search that room properly.","Staying at the inn triggers the Burning House. Finish your shopping first.","Strago rushes in when Relm is trapped and the party goes to rescue her."],[],[],[32],"",null,null,null],["Burning House",1,"Engaging Flame Eater",["Talk to Strago in front of the house, then go in.","Take the FLAME ROD behind the second door on the right and the ICE ROD behind the third.","The Ice Rod is not a souvenir — using it as an item casts a stronger Blizzara that IGNORES MAGIC DEFENSE. That is your best single hit against the boss. It breaks on use, so spend it deliberately.","BALLOON (555 HP, weak to Ice and Water) exists only here. It also comes to the boss fight, where it is a perfect target for Strago's Aqua Breath.","Most enemies inside fold to Blizzara or Aqua Breath in one hit.","Flame Eater (8,400 HP, weak to Ice): Blizzara makes this simple. Terra in Trance casting Blizzara can clear 4,000 depending on her Magic, and the Ice Rod hits harder still.","Steal a Flametongue from it at 87.5%.","Rescuing Relm ends the sequence."],["g13"],[17],[33],"once",null,null,null],["Esper Cave",1,"Reaching the top — this cave and the Sealed Gate both close",["Head west from Thamasa. THIS DUNGEON DOES NOT EXIST IN THE WORLD OF RUIN, and clearing it also permanently closes the Cave to the Sealed Gate. Finish both before you trigger the ending event.","You will see what looks like Relm on the way up. You do not need to chase her.","HEALING ROD is the chest inside the cave. Do not use it as a rod — BET IT AT THE COLOSSEUM later for MAGUS ROD, which carries Magic +7.","The floor with the pit traps has three holes and you drop through them deliberately: UPPER hole for Tabby Suit and Chocobo Suit, RIGHT hole for X-Potion, LOWER-LEFT hole when you are ready to continue.","Bonnacon, Land Grillon, Adamankary, Mandrake and Venobennu are all limited to this cave. Adamankary carries a Golden Shield steal.","At the statues of the Warring Triad, an event plays. Trying to move on afterwards starts Ultros (Esper Caves).","THIS IS NOT A DAMAGE RACE. The data says 22,000 HP, but you only need to deal enough damage for Relm to appear — then use SKETCH to end the battle. He has no Stop resistance, so you can freeze him in place while you wait for the event to advance.","RELM JOINS immediately after this fight — not at Thamasa.","Steal a White Cape from Ultros at 87.5% while you are here.","Reaching the top returns the story to Thamasa automatically."],["g14"],[18],[34],"wob",null,null,null],["Thamasa aftermath and Doma Castle cleanup",1,"",["The story plays out largely on its own back in Thamasa. When control switches to General Leo, you fight Kefka.","Afterwards you board the airship, the Floating Continent rises, and from that point you can CHOOSE to fly there. Nothing forces you up — the world stays open until you commit.","IF YOUR BANQUET SCORE UNLOCKED DOMA CASTLE, go back now. Beyond the Remedy you took during Sabin's scenario, the chests now hold X-Potion, Phoenix Down, PRAYER BEADS, Elixir and Hi-Ether.","If the banquet went badly, Doma's chests are not lost — they are simply delayed to the World of Ruin, which is available either way."],[],[],[35],"",null,null,null],["World of Balance cleanup sweep",1,"Flying to the Floating Continent",["THIS IS THE LAST STOP BEFORE THE WORLD CHANGES. Everything below needs free flight, which you have had since the Maduin flashback and will lose the moment the Floating Continent falls.","WATER HARMONY — the only permanently missable Dance. It cannot be learned in the World of Ruin at all.","Land the airship ON THE VELDT with MOG IN THE PARTY. Enter Crescent Mountain Cave south of the Veldt, jump into the current, and swim the Serpent Trench. The underwater battles are what teach him the Dance.","You come out at Nikeah. Rent a chocobo, ride EAST to Baren Falls, jump down, and you are back at the airship on the Veldt. That is the whole loop.","If you saved Lone Wolf instead of Mog, Water Harmony is gone for this playthrough — Mog can still rejoin in the World of Ruin, but the Dance cannot.","KEY MAGICITE: Seraph (Tzen, 3,000 gil), Zona Seeker (Jidoor auction, 10,000) and Golem (Jidoor auction, 20,000). None is permanently missable, but all three get pushed a long way back if you wait. GOLEM TEACHES STOP, which is what makes Intangir on Triangle Island fightable.","MONSTER SWEEP — encounters change drastically after the Floating Continent. These overworld and island groups all need the airship, so they could not have been done any earlier:","Triangle Island is the hard one. INTANGIR is invisible, immune to almost everything, and counters with Meteor — Stop from Golem is the standard answer.","Crescent Island and the forest west of the Veldt are easy walks from a landed airship; the Southern Continent and desert groups are a slow sweep, so do them on the way between towns.","When the display map shows no gaps left in the World of Balance, take the airship up."],["g15"],[6,22,23,24,25,27,28,30,31,32,33],[],"wob",null,1,null],["Esper Cave leveling",2,"",["Stat espers are live now, so levels stop being free and start being decisions. Everything you held back for is spent here.","Gau to level 26 with ZONA SEEKER equipped for the Magic +2 per level.","Run EXP at 4x for this stretch — the point is to bank the bonuses, not the time.","Deposit Gau on the Veldt afterwards.","From this stop onward, every level-up should have deliberately chosen magicite attached. Strength and Magic never rise on their own in FF6."],["g16"],[],[],"",null,null,null],["Approaching the Floating Continent",3,"Landing",["Choose the Floating Continent from the airship controls when you are ready. You land with UP TO THREE CHARACTERS.","BUY 99 SHURIKEN FIRST if you plan to use Throw — Shadow joins immediately after landing and he is not optional damage up there.","The monsters ahead are much stronger than anything so far. Bring plenty of healing, especially Tents.","You fight around the airship for a while, then Typhon appears and Ultros shows up at the REAR of the airship. Approach him to start the pair fight.","Ultros (17,000 HP, weak to Fire and Poison) and Typhon (10,000 HP, weak to Ice and Water). Terra in Trance casting Fira at Ultros and Blizzara at Typhon does the work. TYPHON CAN BE STOPPED — pin him and delete Ultros first.","AIR FORCE STARTS IMMEDIATELY afterwards, with no chance to regroup.","Air Force (8,000 HP, weak to Lightning and Water): Thundara is the easy answer and Strago's Aqua Breath is excellent. Laser Gun (3,300) and Missile Bay (3,000) share those weaknesses.","BIT CAN ONLY BE REGISTERED HERE, and the way people lose it is by KILLING AIR FORCE TOO FAST. Bit is summoned by Air Force during the fight — hold back your damage until it appears. It is not tied to destroying the Laser Gun.","Bit ABSORBS MAGIC, so kill it with physical attacks.","Steal an X-Ether from the Laser Gun and a Debilitator from the Missile Bay.","Air Force drops a PRINCESS RING at 100%.","After landing, Shadow is lying nearby. Talk to him and he joins."],["g17"],[19],[],"once",null,null,null],["Floating Continent",3,"Approaching the Warring Triad",["The layout looks maze-like but the rule is simple: PRESS EVERY VISIBLE SWITCH.","Check the ITEM SYMBOL EAST OF THE LANDING POINT to fight GIGANTOS. It is a one-time monster and it drops SASUKE at 100% — fight it.","STEAL A GENJI GLOVE FROM DRAGON here. It is a rare steal, but more Dragons only turn up much later in the World of Ruin, so this is your early route to a second dual-wield setup.","Brainpan, Misfit, Apocrypha, Dragon, Platinum Dragon and Behemoth all live only up here. NINJA IS NOT EXCLUSIVE — it also spawns in the Cave to the Sealed Gate and so reaches the Veldt, but this is your last easy shot at it in the World of Balance.","Level Shadow and your Break-caster now; Celes too. Real stats are live and this sweep is much easier than it looks with the magicite bonuses banked.","Deep inside, ULTIMA WEAPON waits. Talk to it to start the fight.","Ultima Weapon (24,000 HP): no weakness, no absorption. Give magic users Earring and physical attackers Gigas Glove or Hyper Wrist, then use everyone's best damage.","IT IS VULNERABLE TO SLOW, which makes the whole fight calmer. Flare Star causes ugly status problems, so put a RIBBON on your healer.","Shadow leaves the party after Ultima Weapon. Continue on for the Kefka and Gestahl event."],["g18"],[20],[36],"once",null,null,null],["Floating Continent escape",3,"Jumping to the Blackjack",["The continent begins collapsing and you have SIX MINUTES to reach the east edge.","NAUDE AND NELAPA ARE TWO DIFFERENT MONSTERS and it is easy to conflate them. NAUDE (3,000 HP, weak to Fire, Lightning and Holy) is the encounter that carries the bestiary entry. NELAPA (2,800 HP) is the boss that attacks when you check the final light.","NAUDE MUST ACTUALLY BE KILLED to register — and killed with ordinary damage. Fire, Lightning or Holy all work. Do NOT finish it with Imp or an instant-death effect, and do not let it escape.","Nelapa itself is straightforward on the way out; just do not spend the timer on it.","At the eastern edge you can board and escape immediately. DO NOT.","CHOOSE TO STAY. Then check toward the airship again and choose to WAIT FOR SHADOW. He arrives with only a few seconds left on the timer.","IF YOU LEAVE WITHOUT WAITING, SHADOW CANNOT REJOIN LATER. This is the single most expensive mistake available in the World of Balance — it costs you a party member for the rest of the game.","Escaping ends the World of Balance."],["g19"],[21],[],"once",null,null,null],["Solitary Island — Cid and the raft",4,"",["The World of Ruin opens with Celes alone at Cid's House. Go south from the house to the beach, catch fish, and feed them to Cid.","CID HAS A HIDDEN HP VALUE. It starts at 120 and drops by 1 every second. He lives if it reaches 256 or more and dies if it reaches 0.","Fish are worth: fastest +32, fast +16, SLOW -4, SLOWEST -16. Only grab the fast ones — a slow fish actively sets you back.","You can read his HP from his dialogue: 'I'm all better now!' is 256+, 'I can feel my strength returning' is 230-255, and 'This is the end for me...' is under 30.","BOTH OUTCOMES LEAD TO THE SAME ITEMS AND THE SAME STORY. Saving Cid is a character moment, not a reward — if you only want to move on, doing nothing is faster.","If Cid lives he tells Celes about the raft in the basement. If he dies, watch the cliff scene, find his letter in the house, and go down beside the stove to reach the raft.","Ride the raft to the northern continent. Albrook is near the landing point."],[],[34],[],"once",null,null,null],["Albrook and the walk north",4,"",["Albrook is a shopping and information stop — the story does not force you inside. People here mention Sabin, which is your lead.","CELES IS STILL ALONE, so overworld battles bite. Keep her in the back row, lean on magic, and run from anything you do not need.","Head north for Tzen when you are ready."],[],[35],[],"",null,null,null],["Tzen — the Crumbling House",4,"Rescuing the child",["Entering Tzen starts the event: the house on the north side is collapsing and Sabin is holding it up.","YOU GO IN WITH CELES ALONE, ON A TIMER. Rescue the child in the basement and get out before it runs out. Succeed and Sabin rejoins.","EQUIP SPRINT SHOES — it is the difference between grabbing every chest and having to choose. Equip a RIBBON too: some enemies inside inflict Petrify, and on a solo Celes that is simply a wipe.","Upper floor: Healing Rod, Ether, Holy Rod, Hyper Wrist. Lower floor: BLOOD SWORD and a Magicite Shard.","THE HOUSE CANNOT BE REVISITED. Zokka, Nightwalker and Scorpion exist only in here.","Afterwards, leave Tzen and go east along the narrow land bridge toward Mobliz."],["g20"],[36],[37],"timed",null,null,null],["Mobliz — Humbaba and Fenrir",4,"",["A child runs out as you enter. Follow it into the basement of the house.","You find Terra underground. The first fight — Terra alone against Humbaba — is SCRIPTED TO END BADLY. Do not spend items trying to win it.","Celes and Sabin then fight Humbaba for real. It has about 28,000 HP here and is weak to Poison. Ignore the bestiary's 60,000 — that number belongs to the first, scripted fight.","SLEEP DOES NOT WORK in this particular fight, though it does in the later ones. Once its HP drops under roughly 20,000 it flees.","Back row for both. Celes spams Cura and Runic to shut down its magic, Sabin uses Aura Cannon. Protect on both helps, and Golem helps more.","You receive the magicite FENRIR. TERRA DOES NOT JOIN YET — you come back for her once you have the airship.","There is a Phoenix Down outside and a Hi-Ether in the basement of the west building.","Head for Nikeah. A hidden Chocobo Stable in the forest just south of Mobliz makes the trip much shorter."],[],[37],[38],"",null,null,null],["Nikeah — the pirates",4,"",["Follow the long land route around from the south and head northwest.","Talk to the pirates in the pub. GERAD then appears near the armor shop — talk to him. He looks exactly like Edgar, because he is.","Follow Gerad to the port and board the ship. It takes you to South Figaro."],[],[],[],"",null,null,null],["South Figaro (World of Ruin)",4,"",["Go to the inn and talk to Gerad on the second floor.","THE SHOPS NOW CARRY THE DIAMOND SERIES. If the last several fights have felt rough, this is the right place to spend — it fixes more than it costs.","The outdoor chests have all rolled over to their final versions: Holy Water, Tent, Phoenix Down, X-Potion, Elixir and Remedy. This is genuinely last chance on these.","Leave town and go southwest to South Figaro Cave."],[],[38],[39],"",null,null,null],["South Figaro Cave (World of Ruin)",4,"",["No boss inside. The far exit is blocked, but THE TURTLE AT THE SPRING carries you across into the Figaro Castle basement.","IF YOU LEFT THE CHESTS ALONE ALL GAME, this is the payoff: 1F holds X-Potion and Hi-Ether, and 2F holds the HERO'S RING that the Thunder Rod chest has been upgrading into since the World of Balance.","These are the final versions — there is no fourth upgrade. Take everything."],[],[],[40],"",null,null,null],["Figaro Castle basement — Edgar returns",4,"",["Head for the engine room at the deepest part. EDGAR REJOINS when you reach the machinery, and the Tentacle fight starts immediately.","All four Tentacles appear at once. Bottom-right 7,000 HP (weak Ice and Water), bottom-left 6,000 (weak Fire), top-right 5,000 (no weakness), top-left 4,000 (no weakness).","Kill the two with elemental weaknesses first using -ra spells — fewer targets makes everything calmer. THE TOP-LEFT ONE CAN BE STOPPED, so freeze its turn early rather than fighting it fair.","After the fight, check the ARMOR in the room beyond the engine room for SOUL SABER.","Sweep the basement: Gravity Rod, Crystal Helm, Hi-Ether and X-Potion on B3F, ROYAL CROWN on B2F.","Talk to the old man on B1F and move the whole castle toward Kohlingen."],[],[39],[41],"",null,null,null],["Kohlingen — finding Setzer",4,"",["Once the castle has moved, go to Kohlingen and talk to Setzer in the pub.","The event points you at Darill's Tomb.","If you never took the Green Beret from the northeast house's back door in the World of Balance, it is still there."],[],[40],[],"",null,null,null],["Darill's Tomb — recovering the Falcon",4,"",["Enter from the WEST side of Kohlingen.","From the first crossroad, go into the UPPER-RIGHT room and inspect the gravestone. The back door opens — then press the switch in that room.","Next take the LOWER-LEFT room from the crossroad and head down to the basement.","IN THE ROOM WITH THE PRINCESS DRESS CHEST there is a hidden passage on the RIGHT side. Follow it to the GROWTH EGG — it doubles EXP for whoever wears it. Do not leave this dungeon without it.","Now go DOWN from the crossroad, press the switch ahead to raise the water level, ride the turtle to the door you opened, and continue.","The chest just above the save point starts ANGLER WHELK. Head 9,230 HP, shell 9,845 HP, both weak to Fire, and BOTH DROP DRAGON CLAWS AT 100%.","Killing either part ends the fight — and gets you only one claw. To take both, wear the head and shell down together and finish them close to simultaneously.","Dullahan waits at the deepest point: 23,450 HP, weak to Fire. Its magic is the danger, so put up Shell. Setzer heals with Cura while Sabin uses Rising Phoenix and Edgar uses Drill.","Setzer recovers THE FALCON. From here the World of Ruin is fully open — you can fly anywhere, including straight to Kefka's Tower if you want a miserable time.","Genji Helm and Crystal Mail on B2F, Regal Gown on B3F alongside the Growth Egg."],["g21"],[41],[42],"",null,null,null],["Duncan's Cabin — Phantom Rush",4,"",["PUT SABIN IN THE PARTY and fly to Duncan's Cabin. The event teaches him PHANTOM RUSH, his final Blitz.","On the world map the cabin looks like a small cluster of FIVE TREES on the northern continent — it is easy to fly straight past.","Phantom Rush is MAGIC-BASED despite appearances, and it ignores Magic Defense. Its base power is high enough that Sabin reaches 9,999 on levels alone.","BECAUSE OF THAT, DO NOT BUILD SABIN AROUND MAGIC. Speed and Strength bonuses age far better for him — the Blitz caps out regardless."],[],[],[],"",null,null,null],["Solitary Island — Quetzalli",4,"",["Fly back to Solitary Island, the island south of Maranda. Go to Cid's House, leave from the south side, and check the beach.","CATCH THE FASTEST FISH to receive the magicite QUETZALLI.","A 2022 Pixel Remaster update gave Quetzalli a SPEED +1 level bonus where it previously had none. Speed is one of the most valuable stats in FF6, so this is worth a dedicated trip rather than a someday-maybe."],[],[],[],"",null,null,null],["Mobliz — Terra rejoins",4,"",["Return to Mobliz with the Falcon. Enter the house in the LOWER-LEFT part of town — a dog slips behind the bookcase and heads into the basement. Follow it.","Humbaba's third fight: 26,000 HP, weak to Poison. SLEEP WORKS THIS TIME. Sabin's Phantom Rush may well out-damage everything else you have.","After enough damage, Humbaba Breath blows TWO RANDOM PARTY MEMBERS out of the fight and ends it.","The fourth fight is Terra plus whichever two stayed in. Same 26,000 HP, same Poison weakness.","Terra is in Trance here — Bio hurts badly if she knows it, otherwise Fira or Thundara. Let her attack while the other two heal and support.","TERRA REJOINS FOR GOOD after this. She is one of the strongest damage dealers in the game, which is the argument for coming back this early rather than later."],[],[],[46],"",null,null,null],["Narshe mines — Mog rejoins",4,"",["Enter Narshe through the mines on the WEST side. From the entrance, go LEFT and inspect the rocky wall to open the hidden mine door, then follow the old moogle route to the moogle room.","Talk to Mog and he rejoins.","THE CHESTS HAVE FINISHED UPGRADING: Elixir, GUARD BRACELET and RIBBON in the mines, plus MOLULU'S CHARM in the moogle room. If you left the Phoenix Down and Sleeping Bag closed back in the prologue, this is the payoff.","MOLULU'S CHARM STOPS RANDOM ENCOUNTERS ENTIRELY while Mog wears it. It makes Cultists' Tower and the second party in Phoenix Cave dramatically easier — pick it up before either.","THE TOWN BUILDINGS ARE STILL LOCKED. Locke has to rejoin before they open, so leave the Narshe treasure sweep for later and come only for Mog now.","Water Harmony had to be learned in the World of Balance. If you missed it, it is gone — nothing here recovers it."],[],[],[47],"",null,null,null],["Narshe cliffs — Valigarmanda",4,"",["Go north through town, enter the NORTHERN mines, take the RIGHT path, and continue toward the cliff where the Battle of Narshe happened.","ICE DRAGON wanders the old defense area — one of the eight dragons. It is skippable for now, but you need all eight for Crusader eventually, so clearing it on this trip saves a return flight.","Go to the snowfield where the frozen esper is and INSPECT IT to fight Valigarmanda.","Valigarmanda (30,000 HP, weak to Fire) attacks with Fire, Ice and Lightning. ELEMENTAL SHIELDS take most of the bite out of the fight, and defense-ignoring attacks are the clean answer on offence.","You receive the VALIGARMANDA magicite, and the path down into Yeti's Cave opens."],[],[48],[],"",null,null,null],["Yeti's Cave — Umaro joins",4,"",["Drop into the cave from the cliff.","MOG MUST BE IN THE PARTY or the recruitment scene simply does not happen. Check before you drop in.","X-Ether on B1F, GAUNTLET on B2F.","Inspect the SKULL CARVING at the deepest point for the MIDGARDSORMR magicite, then the Umaro fight starts.","Umaro (17,200 HP, weak to Fire and Poison) has no tricks — he just hits very hard. Keep HP topped up and burn him down with Fire and your best physical attackers.","Mog talks Umaro into joining afterwards.","The Tonberries formation here carries a MINERVA BUSTIER as both steal and drop if you want to farm it."],[],[49],[49],"",null,null,null],["Maranda — Lola's letter",4,"",["Talk to the woman in the northeast house and read the letter on the desk. Then leave and talk to the PIGEON just west of the house.","The pigeon flies toward Zozo, which is where Cyan's trail leads.","Maranda's World of Ruin shops are good — restock here if you are running low."],[],[47],[],"",null,null,null],["Zozo — buying Rust-Rid",4,"",["Talk to the wandering merchant standing near the inn sign and buy RUST-RID for 1,000 GIL. It is the only way to reach Cyan.","Use it on the RUSTED DOOR on the pub's second floor — the building near the town entrance, above the PUB sign — to reach Mt. Zozo.","If you never set the clock to 6:10:50 for the Chainsaw in the World of Balance, that chest is still sitting there."],[],[],[],"",[["Rust-Rid",1000,"Key item — the only way into Mt. Zozo and therefore to Cyan",""]],null,null],["Mt. Zozo — Cyan rejoins",4,"",["Climb and follow the path. CYAN IS AT THE TOP and rejoins on sight — no fight required.","AFTER HE JOINS, GO BACK TO THE TOP ONCE MORE to find a key. It opens the chest in the previous room. What is inside is Cyan's personal effects rather than a usable reward, but the scene is the point.","STORM DRAGON is optional and NOT required to recruit Cyan. Step on the floor switch near the upper-right of the save point area and a dragon emerges from the nearby chest — touch it to start the fight. You need all eight dragons eventually for Crusader, so take it if the party is ready and leave it if not.","Ice Shield, Red Cap, Thunder Shield and AEGIS SHIELD are on 1F, with a Gold Hairpin outside. That is a serious haul of shields — enough to kit the whole party for elemental fights."],[],[42],[43],"",null,null,null],["The Veldt — Gau rejoins",4,"",["The Veldt is the continent north of Mobliz. Go with ONE TO THREE party members.","After a random battle Gau appears. DO NOTHING AND WAIT — he rejoins on his own. You do NOT need Dried Meat this time.","This is also the natural moment to work on Rage, since the Veldt only rolls monsters you have already registered."],[],[],[],"",null,null,null],["Jidoor (World of Ruin)",4,"",["The shops and the auction stock have both changed for the World of Ruin — check them before moving on.","Your destination is Owzer's Mansion on the north side of town."],[],[],[],"",null,null,null],["Owzer's Mansion — Relm rejoins",4,"",["READ THE ORDERING RULE FIRST. If you WAITED for Shadow on the Floating Continent, you can clear this mansion whenever you like, including before Cave on the Veldt. If you did NOT wait for Shadow, you must first meet Relm at the end of Cave on the Veldt — only then does this become her recruitment event.","Read the diary, then inspect the suspicious painting. Several paintings start battles or open the way forward, so keep checking the odd-looking ones.","EXAMINE THE PAINTING OF EMPEROR GESTAHL TWICE for the EMPEROR'S LETTER — it contains the hint to Phoenix Cave's location.","Chadarnook alternates between a demon form and a goddess form. ATTACK ONLY WHEN THE DEMON IS SHOWING. The goddess form counters healing and support with genuinely nasty effects, so wait it out rather than trying to play through it.","Relm rejoins after the boss.","DO NOT MISS THE BACK ROOM BOOKSHELF — it holds the LAKSHMI magicite.","B1F also has Moogle Suit, Lich Ring, 293 gil, Potion, Ether and Gold Needle."],["g22"],[44],[45],"",null,null,null],["Cultists' Tower — Strago rejoins",4,"",["PUT RELM IN THE PARTY and visit the tower. Strago snaps out of it and rejoins the moment Relm talks to him. That is the entire recruitment — no climbing required.","You can climb now if you want, but THE DUNGEON ONLY ALLOWS MAGIC IN BATTLE and the boss at the top is rough this early.","If you only want the treasure, equip Mog with MOLULU'S CHARM to skip the random battles entirely and save the real clear for later.","The full climb gets its own stop further down this route."],[],[],[],"",null,null,null],["Cave on the Veldt — Behemoth King",4,"",["The cave is in the SOUTHWEST part of the Veldt.","SHADOW CAN ONLY BE RECOVERED IF YOU WAITED FOR HIM ON THE FLOATING CONTINENT. If you left without him, he is gone for the rest of the game and this cave is just treasure plus the Relm trigger.","Interceptor is near the entrance — follow him deeper.","DO NOT MISS THE ICHIGEKI on B2F. You need it at the Colosseum to get Shadow back, and there is no second copy.","Berserker Ring is on 1F.","Behemoth King is TWO FIGHTS BACK TO BACK. The second form is UNDEAD, so revival items and Holy damage delete it quickly.","The party moves to Thamasa automatically afterwards."],[],[43],[44],"",null,null,null],["Thamasa (World of Ruin)",4,"",["Nothing is required here beyond shopping.","If you never found the MEMENTO RING in Relm's room on 2F — hidden around the left wall near the left side of the table — it is still available.","This is the branch point for the two recruitment orders: with Shadow saved, bet Ichigeki at the Colosseum next. Without him, Owzer's Mansion is now open for Relm instead."],[],[],[],"",null,null,null],["Colosseum — Shadow rejoins",4,"",["BET ICHIGEKI at the Colosseum. Shadow appears as your opponent — win and he rejoins permanently.","He joins after the battle either way, but IF YOU LOSE, THE ICHIGEKI IS GONE. Bring a party that can actually win.","If Shadow was not saved on the Floating Continent this event never triggers at all.","Siegfried (Coliseum) is a Colosseum-only bestiary entry, and he does NOT just show up — YOU MUST BET A MEGALIXIR to draw him out. He is a separate entry from the Siegfried on the Phantom Train. Winning returns a Tintinnabulum."],[],[57],[],"",null,null,null],["Phoenix Cave — Locke rejoins",4,"",["Land the airship in the HOLLOW IN THE MOUNTAINS NORTH OF TZEN.","THIS DUNGEON NEEDS TWO PARTIES. One of them fights RED DRAGON, so put your stronger team there.","Give the other party MOG WITH MOLULU'S CHARM to shut off random battles entirely while it works the switches.","There are a lot of switches and the two parties gate each other's progress. Follow the map alongside the notes rather than trying to hold the layout in your head.","Locke rejoins at the end and you receive the PHOENIX magicite.","MOST OF THE CHESTS IN HERE ARE GENUINELY EMPTY AND THAT IS NOT A BUG — Locke had already looted them. He hands the contents over during the Kohlingen scene: X-Potion, Phoenix Down, X-Ether, Elixir, FLAME SHIELD and the VALIANT KNIFE. None of it is missable and there is nothing to return for. The four real chests are Wing Edge, Teleport Stone, Dragon Horn and the Ribbon past the drained lava."],[],[45],[53],"",null,null,null],["Narshe — treasure cleanup, Ragnarok and the Cursed Shield",4,"",["WITH LOCKE BACK, the locked houses in Narshe finally open. This is the cleanup trip you deferred earlier.","THE RAGNAROK CHOICE: LOCKE MUST BE IN THE PARTY or the event will not fire. Go into the weapon shop and talk to the old man in the room behind the counter. He offers the RAGNAROK MAGICITE or the RAGNAROK SWORD. You get one and the other is gone forever — SAVE FIRST.","The MAGICITE teaches Ultima and grants Metamorphose. The SWORD has 255 Attack with strong stat boosts and can be bet at the Colosseum for LIGHTBRINGER.","BE REALISTIC ABOUT METAMORPHOSE. It succeeds 1 time in 8, and then picks one of four items at random — so any specific item is roughly a 1-in-32 roll. It is not a farming engine.","Most of what it can produce is easier to get another way: Ribbon is a simpler steal from Brachiosaur, Elixir a rare steal from Peeper, and Genji Glove comes from chests and Floating Continent Dragon steals. The one genuine use is extra SAFETY BIT copies off Clymenus in the Phoenix Cave, since those are otherwise limited — the only others are the single 8F chest in the Cultists' Tower and a 12.5% steal from Fiend in Kefka's Tower.","Ultima is also learnable from Paladin's Shield, so the magicite is not your only route to it either.","There is no objectively correct answer here — take the one you actually want to use.","CURSED SHIELD: LOCKE MUST BE IN THE PARTY here too. Climb to the house northeast of the relic shop and the man there hands it over. It is genuinely awful at first and inflicts a pile of statuses.","FIGHT 256 BATTLES WITH IT EQUIPPED and it becomes PALADIN'S SHIELD, one of the best shields in the game. Start the count now — 256 battles is a long tail, and every battle you fight before starting is a battle wasted.","Also sweep the Elixirs in the northeast and northwest buildings and anything left in the southeast storehouse."],["g25"],[],[48],"",null,null,null],["Zone Eater's Belly — Gogo joins",4,"",["Fly to TRIANGLE ISLAND and let ZONE EATER swallow the party. That is the only entrance.","BRING SOMEONE WHO CAN CAST TELEPORT. The dungeon does not eject you after Gogo joins, and walking the whole thing back out is miserable.","In the room where men walk back and forth on bridges, touching one knocks you to the lower floor. THERE IS TREASURE DOWN THERE — fall on purpose at least once.","AFTER THE SAVE POINT THE CEILING STARTS DROPPING. Stand in the gaps. If it lands on you it is an instant game over, so SAVE RIGHT BEFORE THAT ROOM.","B2F holds Genji Armor, Magical Brush and Fake Mustache. The bridge fall leads to Red Jacket and Hi-Ether. Past the ceiling room are Zephyr Cloak, Hero's Ring and Pinwheel, with a Thunder Shield before the deepest room.","Talk to Gogo at the deepest point and he joins."],[],[50,52],[51],"",null,1,null],["Opera House — Earth Dragon",4,"",["One of the eight dragons is waiting here in the World of Ruin.","Go up to the SECOND FLOOR, enter the NORTHEAST room, and pull the SECOND SWITCH FROM THE RIGHT. The party drops onto the stage and the fight starts immediately — there is no chance to re-equip, so set up first.","Earth Dragon (28,500 HP, weak to Water and Wind). Almost everything dangerous it does is Earth-elemental: Quake, Landslide, Magnitude 8.","EQUIP GAIA GEAR FROM NIKEAH AND THOSE ATTACKS HEAL YOU INSTEAD. That single swap turns the fight around more than any damage upgrade would.","It also has no Sleep resistance, so Sleep makes it far less messy.","It ALWAYS drops the MAGUS ROD — Magic +7, and one of the best rods in the game. Relm, Strago or Gogo will want it. (Some guides call it the Wizard Rod; Magus Rod is the Pixel Remaster name, and it is the same rod the Healing Rod bet wins you at the Colosseum.)"],[],[],[],"",null,null,null],["Cave to the Ancient Castle",4,"",["Talk to the old man on B1F of Figaro Castle and move the castle between Figaro and Kohlingen. Partway through, it CATCHES ON SOMETHING UNDERGROUND.","CHOOSE TO STOP, then leave through the prison area on the RIGHT side of B1F. That is the entrance to the cave.","Mostly a corridor to the Ancient Castle, but open the chest at the end of the LOWER-RIGHT path to fight MASTER TONBERRY.","Master Tonberry (22,000 HP) always drops GLADIUS — the strongest dagger in the game by Attack. It is skippable, and it should not be.","IT HAS NO SLEEP RESISTANCE. Put it to sleep, then kill it with MAGIC ONLY — physical attacks wake it up.","Chests along the way: Wing Edge, Hi-Ether, Death Tarot, X-Potion and a Magicite Shard."],[],[],[],"",null,null,null],["Ancient Castle — Odin, Raiden and Blue Dragon",4,"Fleeing Samurai Soul",["ENTER FROM THE LEFT DOORWAY OUTSIDE FIRST. The chest inside starts SAMURAI SOUL.","Samurai Soul (37,620 HP, weak to Poison) drops MASTER'S SCROLL at 100% — the relic that turns Attack into four hits, and one of the best things in the game. Edgar's Noiseblaster can confuse it, which defuses most of the fight.","DO NOT RUN FROM IT. Fleeing costs you the Master's Scroll and the bestiary entry, and the chest does not reset.","If it starts throwing weapons the damage spikes hard, so bring real damage — Phantom Rush closes it quickly.","In the throne room, inspect the STATUE OF ODIN for the ODIN magicite.","From the RIGHT-HAND THRONE as you see it, walk FIVE STEPS DOWN and check the floor. A hidden switch opens stairs in the room to the right.","Downstairs is BLUE DRAGON (26,900 HP, weak to Lightning) — dragon number five. Terra in Trance with Thundaga caps out easily; any Thundaga user does the job while the rest heal.","IN THAT SAME UNDERGROUND ROOM, inspect the QUEEN STATUE to change Odin into RAIDEN. THIS CANNOT BE UNDONE.","Make the change. In the Pixel Remaster, Raiden's level bonus is SPEED +2 — the old reason to hoard Odin for Speed growth no longer exists, and Odin's Meteor can be learned from Doomsday anyway.","Also collect Punisher in the 1F east room, Blizzard Orb and Gold Hairpin in the room right of the throne, and an X-Ether in the hidden room."],["g23"],[54],[52],"",null,null,null],["Cultists' Tower — the full climb",4,"",["One of the roughest dungeons in the game. IN BATTLE YOU CAN ONLY USE MAGIC AND ITEMS — no Attack, no Tools, no Blitz. Going in half-prepared is genuinely miserable.","LEARN RERAISE BEFORE YOU CLIMB. This is not optional advice. MAGIC MASTER CASTS ULTIMA WHEN IT DIES, and that can wipe a party that already won the fight. A Reflect Ring does NOT stop it — Reflect bounces its regular casting, not the death counter.","PUT MOG IN THE PARTY WITH MOLULU'S CHARM. Random encounters disappear entirely and the climb stops draining your HP and MP before the bosses. Fixed fights still happen.","Several enemies here start with Reflect, which is maddening in a magic-only tower. Meteor and Ultima are non-elemental and far less fiddly than trying to bounce spells off your own party.","Climb the stairs and check each side room. In the FIRST stair section there is a HIDDEN FLOOR SWITCH beside the Safety Bit chest — press it and a door opens ONE FLOOR BELOW containing Air Anchor.","The chest list by floor: Safety Bit on 8F, Air Anchor on 7F, Genji Shield on 17F, Kagenui on 26F, Force Armor on 35F, Soul of Thamasa on 39F.","HOLY DRAGON is in the side room with the Kagenui chest — dragon number six. 18,500 HP, and NO SILENCE RESISTANCE, so Silence makes the fight trivial.","BRING LOCKE OR GOGO AND STEAL FROM HOLY DRAGON BEFORE YOU KILL IT. It drops nothing at all — the HOLY LANCE is a 12.5% steal and the common steal is an X-Potion, so keep stealing until you get it. The dragon does not come back, so a clean kill with no thief present costs you the lance for the run.","At the top, open the chest for Soul of Thamasa. TRYING TO LEAVE triggers Magic Master.","Magic Master (50,000 HP) uses Barrier Change to keep rotating its weakness. Chasing the weakness is a losing game — set Reraise, use Carbuncle or a Reflect Ring for its ordinary casting, and finish it with Ultima, Meteor or any strong non-elemental damage."],[],[55],[54],"",null,null,null],["Ebot's Rock — Grand Delta",4,"",["PUT STRAGO AND RELM IN THE PARTY and go to Thamasa. An event near the town entrance opens the way. Without both of them nothing happens.","Leave town afterwards and Ebot's Rock appears on the SMALL ISLAND JUST NORTH OF THAMASA.","Visibility inside is terrible. Step on the floor switches to warp around and open chests. EVERY CHEST HERE CONTAINS CORAL.","A TALKING CHEST blocks the path and wants 22 PIECES OF CORAL. GIVE ALL 22 AT ONCE — if you feed it in small batches it never fills up. This is the mistake that makes people think the dungeon is bugged.","Enemies here often drop Teleport Stone, so leaving is easy if you need to restock.","Hidon (25,000 HP, weak to Fire and Holy) comes with four Erebus parts at 3,500 HP each, all with different weaknesses.","KILL ALL FOUR EREBUS PARTS FIRST. Hidon can only use GRAND DELTA once it is alone — and Strago seeing that cast is the entire point of the fight. Do not kill Hidon early.","IF YOU MISS IT, IT IS RECOVERABLE. Talk to GUNGHO in Thamasa afterwards; there is a 1-in-8 chance he says Hidon has returned. When he does, fly back and fight it again."],[],[56],[59],"",null,null,null],["Doma Castle and the Dreamscape",4,"Defeating Wrexsoul",["PUT CYAN IN THE PARTY and sleep in the bedroom at Doma Castle.","GRAB THE DOMA CASTLE TREASURE FIRST. By now the castle chests can all be collected normally regardless of how the banquet went: X-Potion, Phoenix Down, Prayer Beads, Elixir and Hi-Ether, plus the Remedy from Sabin's scenario.","DREAMSCAPE CANNOT BE RE-ENTERED once cleared, and eleven monsters live only inside it: Samurai, Al Jabr, Suriander, Weredragon, Schmidt, Pluto Armor, Alluring Rider, Pandora, Parasite, Coco and Io.","PHANTOM AREA: you start alone. Of the three doors in a row, the LEFT door leads to your first party member. From there take the upper-right door, upper-right again, then the RIGHT door for the second member. From that spot, go through the upper-left door and then the door to the LEFT for the boss.","Curlax (15,000 HP, weak Ice and Water, sleepable), Laragorn (10,000 HP, weak Fire, dies to Death) and Moebius (12,500 HP, no weakness, stoppable). CURLAX CAN REVIVE THE OTHERS WITH ARISE — put it to sleep or kill it first.","PHANTOM TRAIN AREA: the first car is a pass-through. In the next car, pull the RIGHT LEVER TWICE to reach the Genji Glove.","For the moving chest blocking Flame Shield, take the LUMP OF METAL from the upper-left chest and put it into the moving chest.","MEMORISE THE SIX-CHEST PATTERN, then set the later six to match: close the upper-right chest, and close the lower-left and lower-middle chests. Pull the lever above them to continue.","In the engine car, set ALL THREE LEVERS DOWN and go outside.","CAVE AREA: enter from the upper-right outside path, then immediately go back out — you reappear near the bridge. Cross it and the party falls into the Doma Castle area.","DOMA CASTLE AREA: there is a save point and a full HP/MP recovery bucket. Head to the throne room for Wrexsoul.","Wrexsoul (23,066 HP, weak to Ice) HIDES INSIDE ONE OF YOUR OWN PARTY MEMBERS and you cannot tell which. KO your characters ONE AT A TIME — if Wrexsoul appears, attack it; if not, revive that character and try the next.","CYAN LEARNS EVERY BUSHIDO TECHNIQUE after the fight.","GO BACK TO THE THRONE ROOM afterwards for the ALEXANDER magicite. In the Pixel Remaster it carries Strength +2, so it is a real pickup and not just a collectible."],["g24"],[53],[50],"once",null,null,null],["Deathgaze and the eight dragons",4,"",["DEATHGAZE is a roaming encounter on the world map. In the Pixel Remaster it is VISIBLE as you fly, so hunting it is far less painful than it used to be.","Deathgaze (55,555 HP, weak to Fire and Holy) FLEES MID-BATTLE, BUT ITS DAMAGE CARRIES OVER between encounters. Keep chasing and it eventually falls — you do not need to win in one pass.","IT USES LV.5 DEATH. Do not bring characters whose level is a multiple of 5. That one check prevents most of the disasters in this fight.","Around level 40 is comfortable. The reward is the BAHAMUT magicite.","THE EIGHT DRAGONS award DOOMSDAY when all are defeated. Six are reachable now: Storm Dragon (Mt. Zozo), Ice Dragon (Narshe, past the northern mines), Earth Dragon (Opera House), Red Dragon (Phoenix Cave), Blue Dragon (Ancient Castle) and Holy Dragon (Cultists' Tower).","THE LAST TWO — Gold Dragon and Skull Dragon — ARE INSIDE KEFKA'S TOWER, so Doomsday necessarily completes in the final dungeon. Clear the first six before you go in or you will be backtracking through the tower.","Odin's Meteor can be learned from Doomsday, which is why changing Odin to Raiden costs you nothing."],[],[51],[],"",null,null,null],["Dinosaur Forest — leveling",4,"",["The forest NORTH OF THE VELDT on the world map. It is not a separate dungeon — it is the overworld forest tile.","Equip GROWTH EGG on whoever you want to raise. It doubles their EXP and this is the only place where that multiplier really pays.","Tyrannosaur and Brachiosaur are ordinary encounters here that hit like bosses. If you have Ultima, one strong character can solo them; a Master's Scroll setup works too.","BRACHIOSAUR CAN DROP CELESTRIAD at 12.5%, which reduces every spell's MP cost to 1. THE COLOSSEUM CHAIN RUNS TOWARD IT, NOT AWAY: bet a SOUL OF THAMASA to win a Celestriad. Betting a Celestriad gets you a Dragon Horn instead, so do not bet one you want to keep.","Target at least THREE characters at level 60 or higher before the final dungeon. Kefka's Tower splits you three ways, and a weak third party is where runs fall apart.","The Pixel Remaster's EXP boosters shorten this considerably if you are using them."],[],[46],[],"",null,null,null],["Before the final battle — the audit",4,"Entering Kefka's Tower",["CHECK ALL 14 CHARACTERS ARE AVAILABLE. The tower splits three ways, so a missing member hurts more here than anywhere else in the game.","Terra: the later Mobliz Humbaba event. Locke: clear Phoenix Cave. Edgar: Figaro Castle basement. Sabin: Tzen's Crumbling House. Celes: starts the World of Ruin. Cyan: Mt. Zozo after Maranda's letter. Setzer: Kohlingen, then Darill's Tomb.","Gau: take three or fewer to the Veldt and wait after a battle. Mog: the moogle room in Narshe Mines. Strago: bring Relm to Cultists' Tower. Relm: clear Owzer's Mansion. Umaro: beat Yeti with Mog in the party. Gogo: Zone Eater's Belly from Triangle Island.","SHADOW IS THE ONLY ONE THAT CAN BE PERMANENTLY LOST — and only if you did not wait for him on the Floating Continent. If you did wait: clear Cave on the Veldt, then bet Ichigeki at the Colosseum.","MAGICITE CHECK — Odin becomes Raiden irreversibly at the Ancient Castle; Doomsday requires all eight dragons and therefore finishes inside the tower.","GEAR CHECK — Paladin's Shield if your 256 Cursed Shield battles are done, Flame Shield for Meltdown healing setups, Genji Shield for straight defence.","This is the last point where anything outside the tower is still reachable."],[],[],[],"",null,null,null],["Kefka's Tower — first half",4,"",["THE THREE-PARTY SPLIT IS DECIDED HERE AND THE FIRST-HALF ROUTES ARE FIXED, so your split chooses who fights what.","PARTY 1 (left) has NO BOSS in the first half — it is the right home for weaker characters. Do not make it helpless though; it still has to clear a Warring Triad route in the second half.","PUT STRAGO IN PARTY 1 OR PARTY 3 IF YOU WANT FORCE FIELD. Fiend is the only enemy that teaches it, and depending on the route Fiend is fought by Party 1 or Party 3. PARTY 2 CAN NEVER FIGHT FIEND.","KNOW WHICH ONES ACTUALLY NEED A THIEF. Guaranteed 100% drops — Fiend gives MUTSUNOKAMI, Demon gives RADIANT LANCE, Goddess gives EXCALIBUR — so those need nobody. The steals are the scarce half: Guardian has Force Armor at 87.5% and RIBBON at 12.5%, Demon has RED JACKET, Fiend has SAFETY BIT, Goddess has MINERVA BUSTIER, all at 12.5%. Put Locke or Gogo on the route whose steals you want; you can steal, Teleport out, and come back through another route for more.","Start with Party 1. When you reach a room where the floor is missing and you cannot continue, switch to Party 2.","Party 2 reaches a room with toilets. ULTIMA BUSTER is in the far-left room — 55,000 HP, no weakness, heavy magic user. It is OPTIONAL, but beating it creates a save point. Shell and high Magic Defence help, and Reraise covers its Ultima.","From there go down to the outside area with Force Armor and Force Shield, take the CENTER passage, and step on the floor switch. That moves the floor for Party 1.","Switch to Party 1, cross the new path, and go as far as the glowing chest. Then switch back to Party 2.","With Party 2, go back one screen to the outside area and take the RIGHT path. GOLD DRAGON is here — 32,400 HP, weak to Water, and it leans on Lightning damage, so a Thunder Shield blunts most of it. Continue and stand on the next floor switch.","Switch to Party 3. It fights INFERNO shortly after the save point: 30,800 HP, weak to Lightning, ABSORBS FIRE. Rahu has 8,000 HP and Ketu has 11,000.","DO NOT KILL INFERNO'S ARMS FIRST — losing them lets Inferno raise a Magitek Barrier, gain Reflect and start casting Meteor. Hit the body with Thundaga and end it fast.","Keep Party 3 moving and check the glowing chest in the lower-left outside area — that opens Party 1's route. SKULL DRAGON is also on this route: 32,800 HP, weak to Fire and Holy, and it throws status effects, so Ribbon helps.","IF THE OTHER SEVEN DRAGONS ARE DONE, Skull Dragon awards DOOMSDAY.","Push each party as far as it can go until all three meet on the same large floor."],["g26"],[58],[55,56,57],"",null,null,null],["Kefka's Tower — second half",4,"",["WHICH SIDE THE CENTER PARTY TAKES FIRST DECIDES EVERY BOSS ASSIGNMENT. Go LEFT first and it is Party 1 Fiend, Party 2 Goddess, Party 3 Guardian and Demon. Go RIGHT first and it is Party 1 Goddess, Party 2 Guardian and Demon, Party 3 Fiend.","CHOOSE THAT DIRECTION DELIBERATELY — it is how you put Strago on Fiend for Force Field and Locke on the steals you want.","With the left and right parties on their switches, the center party can cross the middle. Send it left or right, DROP THE 4-TON WEIGHT, and that locks one switch in place.","Once both side weights are down, move the side parties on and have ALL THREE stand on the three switches in the back room. A path opens in the center.","Guardian (60,000 HP, weak to Lightning and Water) CAN CAST ULTIMA — burst it with Thundaga, or set Reraise if the fight is dragging. It drops nothing; Force Armor 87.5% and Ribbon 12.5% are steals.","Demon (58,000 HP, weak to Poison): Poison damage options are thin, so strong non-elemental attacks like Ultima are simpler. Fire protection blunts Firaga and Flare Star. RADIANT LANCE is a guaranteed drop; Red Jacket is the 12.5% steal.","Fiend (63,000 HP, weak to Holy): FORCE FIELD CAN RANDOMLY NULLIFY AN ELEMENT, so non-elemental damage is the safer plan even though Holy is the listed weakness. This is where Strago learns Force Field. MUTSUNOKAMI is a guaranteed drop; Safety Bit is the 12.5% steal.","Goddess (44,000 HP, no weakness) throws heavy status effects and can charm your characters. Keep recovery close and do not let it drag. EXCALIBUR is a guaranteed drop; Minerva Bustier is the 12.5% steal.","After each boss, push that party to its deepest switch. When all three are standing on the final switches, the path to the last battle opens.","There is one more Ribbon in the outside area of the second half."],[],[],[58],"",null,null,null],["The final battle",4,"",["THE LAST FIGHT IS FOUR TIERS. You order 12 characters first, and the first four start. As each tier ends, ANY KO'D CHARACTERS LEAVE THE FIGHT and the next in line step in.","PUT YOUR STRONGEST CHARACTERS NEAR THE FRONT of that order.","BEFORE ENDING EACH TIER, GET EVERYONE BACK ON THEIR FEET. A character who happens to be KO'd when a tier ends is swapped out for the next fight — that is how people lose their best damage dealer halfway up.","Tier 1 is Statue of the Gods A, B and C. Tier 2 is Statue of the Gods D, E, F and G.","Work up through the remaining tiers to Kefka himself."],[],[],[],"",null,null,null]];
